{
  "_comment": "The Test extension's manifest vocabulary: what a manifest may write inside the mapping it binds to this file -- what the extension's actions must print. Bound the way Map/manifest-context.jsonld explains: a term of the manifest's choosing (tst:parms, say) whose property-scoped @context is this file's URL, declared beside the prefix in the manifest's @context -- `tst: http://shex.io/extensions/Test/#` and, beside it, `tst:parms: {@context: https://shexspec.github.io/extensions/Test/manifest-context.jsonld}` -- and never imported at the top level. prints is the list of lines the extension's print(...) actions emit when the entry is validated, in the order they emit them; the ShEx conformance suite's semantic-action tests, which used to say this with the test vocabulary's extensionResults, say it here. A member is the line, as a string, when the action that printed it was dispatched on the extension's own IRI, http://shex.io/extensions/Test/; an action dispatched on another IRI in this namespace -- the suite's http://shex.io/extensions/Test/#a, #b and #c, which exercise the order of externally supplied actions -- writes a node, {extension: <that IRI>, line: <the line>}. A line printed by fail(...) is a line like any other; whether the entry conforms is its status. Every name maps to an absolute IRI under http://shex.io/extensions/Test/# (the extension's actions are dispatched on http://shex.io/extensions/Test/, without the #, as ShExReduce's are), and this file declares no prefix and nothing outside the scope, so it cannot collide with another vocabulary, whatever prefix the manifest chose for it. Outer names stay visible inside the scope, so shex.js's pluginURL, naming the web-app plugin that implements this extension, is written inside the mapping too. Stacked, in a manifest, onto the ShEx manifest vocabulary (https://www.w3.org/ns/shex-manifest.jsonld) and whatever terms the manifest's author adds to it (shex.js's are https://shex.js.org/doc/manifest-context.jsonld; the conformance suite's are https://www.w3.org/ns/shex-test.jsonld).",

  "@context": {
    "prints": {"@id": "http://shex.io/extensions/Test/#prints", "@container": "@list"},
    "extension": {"@id": "http://shex.io/extensions/Test/#extension", "@type": "@id"},
    "line": "http://shex.io/extensions/Test/#line"
  }
}
